    "prompt": "In \"The Volcano,\" the audience knows from the first moment something Dev does not. Write an essay that explains how this dramatic irony creates both suspense and humor in the scene. Analyze at least two moments, quoting dialogue or stage directions, and explain how the gap between what the audience knows and what Dev knows makes each moment tense or funny. End by explaining how the gap closes, and why the playwright has Anika reveal the truth herself instead of having Dev discover it.",
